<title>UK: SWIMMING-EUROPEAN SHORT-COURSE RECORD FOR BRITAIN'S HICKMAN.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-EUROPEAN SHORT-COURSE RECORD FOR BRITAIN'S HICKMAN.</headline>
<dateline>GLASGOW 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>James Hickman of Britain set a European short-course record for the men's 100 metres butterfly when he clocked 52.34 seconds at a World Cup meeting on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Hickman beat the mark of 52.51 set by Michael Gross of Germany in Aachen on March 10, 1990, and equalled by Denis Silantiev of Ukraine in Espoo, Finland, on January 23 this year.</p>
